/-!
# Schwinger--Dyson non-renormalization in Chern--Simons theory

This file formalizes the central argument of D. Daniel and N. Dorey,
*The Schwinger--Dyson equations and non-renormalization in Chern--Simons theory*,
Physics Letters B **246** (1990), 82--86.

* **# A** differentiates the vector-supersymmetry Ward functional (Eq. 5) through its two- and
  three-point Fréchet insertions (Eqs. 6--7), proves the `SU(2)` adjoint-Casimir color contraction,
  proves the Levi-Civita contraction of the three-vector vertex decomposition (Eq. 13), packages
  the Ward-reduced ghost and gauge Schwinger--Dyson equations (14) and (19), and derives the
  vanishing residual `C(k,q)` vertex integral (Eq. 20).
* **# B** proves the Fubini and `p -> k-p` identity converting Eqs. (21)--(22) into the radial
  continuum constraint (Eq. 23). Scale invariance then makes the dimensionless wave-function
  factor constant, and non-integrability of `p^2` proves `H = 1` at positive momentum (Eq. 24),
  hence its momentum beta function vanishes there.
* **# C** constructs the displayed bare ghost scalar and transverse Levi-Civita gauge tensor,
  proves the exact dressed versions are bare, and connects the vanished Ward kernel to the
  repository's continuum Dyson--Schwinger propagator.
* **# D** keeps the gauge-invariant-regulator branch honest: when the vector supersymmetry Ward
  identity is anomalous, the repository's existing boundary carrier gives the finite adjoint-trace
  level shift instead of a zero-renormalization claim.

The paper's function-space statement `p d(p^2) [H(p^2)-1]` is represented after the exact change
of variables `d(p^2) = 2 p dp` by `2 p^2 (H(p^2)-1) dp` on the positive half-line.

**Honest scope.** The functional Ward hierarchy takes the unbroken Eq. (5) identity and its Fréchet
regularity as inputs, then proves its differentiated consequences; it does not construct Eq. (5)
from a gauge-fixed functional measure. `DanielWardSchwingerDysonData` starts after the arbitrary
semisimple group-index reduction: its kernels are the contracted loop integrals appearing in
Eqs. (14) and (19). The color contraction is computed here for `SU(2)`; other groups require their
own adjoint-Casimir identity. The Levi-Civita/momentum contraction and the six-dimensional
Fubini/momentum-shift step are proved;
`DanielFubiniMomentumShiftData` still takes the paper-specific Eqs. (21) and (22) and their
integrability as inputs. The continuum adapter reuses a scalar external-field Dyson carrier and is
not a construction of distribution-valued gauge/ghost tensor propagators. No claim is made for
higher-point non-renormalization, which the paper presents only as a possible extension.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 100000

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

